    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Anonymized dataset of 61 drivers who completed a 25.8 km (16 mi) loop through freeway, suburban, and urban driving settings.  Each driver answered the randomly posed question “Is now a good time?” when verbally prompted by an automatic system, ~ every 30-90 seconds. Contextual information was collected using an instrumented 2016 Toyota Prius V. The data capture system included multi-channel video of the cabin and road, vehicle telemetry, GPS position, inertial forces, and driver physiological data. Some data is missing due to technical issues in capture; 45 drivers have complete data sets. Refer to associated publications for data capture details. Dataset only includes data from participants who consented to public distribution of data. Faces are blurred in video; please contact authors about how to gain access to non-anonymized dataset if needed.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Martelaro, N. and Ju, W. (2022). Is Now A Good Time? Dataset for Modelling  Vehicle-Driver Communication Timing . Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/gj863qr6417",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
